\section{Conclusion}
In this letter, we propose a diffusion-based aircraft target detection
network for SAR images named DiffDet4SAR, presentING a first study that introduces diffusion models to SAR target detection. We formulated aircraft target detection as a spatial generation task of the position and size of bounding boxes. Furthermore, to address the discrete nature of scattered points from aircraft targets and strong background interference, we designed the SFE module to capture texture details and semantic information as a means of enhancing target saliency and suppressing background clutter. The experimental results presented herein have demonstrated the effectiveness of the proposed DiffDet4SAR method. 

